; fas9_coordination_xref.scr - facit script of step 9.6 (F9.23 coordination model and xref panels). Run it with
;   python -I tools/fas9_facit_run.py doc/facit/fas9_coordination_xref.scr
; It makes its own xref source: a rectangle, a circle and a text are drawn, written with -WBLOCK to fas9_xref_source.dwg (in the
; directory the facit run writes to; the objects are deleted by -WBLOCK), and that drawing is attached as an xref. Then one change
; per file: rotation and mirror of the xref's INSERT (a mirror is a negative scale), unload, reload, a changed path, detach.
;
; What AutoCAD 2025's core cannot do, and what is therefore "ej testat" (plan 2026-10-27-fas-9-typer.md, F9.23):
;   COORDINATION_MODEL / NAVISWORKSMODELDEF (-COORDINATIONMODELATTACH exists in the core but opens only a REAL Navisworks model:
;     "<file> does not point to a valid model file" for an NWD that is any other file, and the prompt then repeats until the
;     script's lines are used up); NWCOUT, which could make an NWC from a drawing, is not in the core; no real NWD/NWC is in the
;     corpus or on the web (searched 2026-10-28: only format descriptions). So there is no AutoCAD record of a coordination model
;     and no 16 + 1 values of code 40, no two 290 of the definition, no ACAD_BIM_DEFINITIONS entry from AutoCAD: the groups are
;     Autodesk's 2018 DXF reference's and what AutoCAD's core accepted in phase 6 (B78).
;     When a real model is at doc/facit/coordination.nwd, the lines below (comments) make the files: remove the semicolons.
;   XREFPANELOBJECT / EXACXREFPANELOBJECT: no AutoCAD file has a record of either (the core's -XREF does not make one; the class
;     EXACXREFPANELOBJECT, "ExAcXREFPanelObject" of the application EXAC_ESW, is only registered in CLASSES of every AutoCAD file);
;     the objects belong to the External References palette of the AutoCAD user interface, which the core does not have, and
;     Autodesk's DXF reference does not document them. Their grammar is not established: HDxf keeps such a record as it is.
;
; ;_.-COORDINATIONMODELATTACH
; ;coordination.nwd
; ;0,0,0
; ;1
; ;0
; ;;SAVE coordination
; ;_.ROTATE
; ;_ALL
; ;
; ;0,0
; ;30
; ;;SAVE coordination rotated
;
; Plain AutoCAD commands, no LISP. ;SAVE saves R12, 2000, 2004, 2007, 2010, 2013 and 2018, ASCII and binary.
_.RECTANG
0,0
60,40
_.CIRCLE
30,20
10
_.TEXT
5,5
5
0
XREF SOURCE
_.-WBLOCK
fas9_xref_source.dwg

0,0,0
_ALL

_.-XREF
_A
fas9_xref_source.dwg
0,0,0
1
1
0
;EXPECT INSERT
;SAVE xref
_.ROTATE
_ALL

0,0
30
;SAVE xref rotated
_.MIRROR
_ALL

0,50
100,50
_Y
;SAVE xref mirrored
_.-XREF
_U
fas9_xref_source
;SAVE xref unloaded
_.-XREF
_R
fas9_xref_source
_.-XREF
_P
fas9_xref_source
.\fas9_xref_source.dwg
;SAVE xref path_changed
_.-XREF
_D
fas9_xref_source
;SAVE xref detached
